Assuming you mean Bending Spoons (Nasdaq: BSP), the latest reported sharp gap-up was driven mainly by enthusiasm around financing for its planned Miro acquisition—not by a confirmed new announcement on the day of the jump.

The company closed add-ons to its term loans: $1.25 billion and €395 million, due in 2031. Investors viewed the financing, along with credit-rating upgrades from Moody’s and S&P, as reducing uncertainty about funding the Miro deal and supporting further acquisitions. The stock surged about 24% in that session.

